{"id":"int-0cb8bce4","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-05-15T14:47:44.417548407Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-2qz","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"Added Event.last_seen_at through a migration, bumped it in the metrics writer (monotonic, ignores count=0), added silent_since_days API filtering, added the Last seen catalog column (hidden by default with bootstrap), and added Silent > 1d/7d/30d toolbar options. Tests: 161 backend, 31 frontend, ruff and mypy clean."}}
{"id":"int-237c172e","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-05-15T18:53:22.869316405Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-wtu","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"alerting_matching.py: pure rule_matches_anomaly plus simulate_rule_firings with in-memory cooldown and per-scope partitioning. The metrics worker uses the same path. Added POST /alert-destinations/{id}/rules/{id}/simulate?days=N and Pydantic schemas. UI: History button on each rule plus RuleReplayDialog with firings table and noisy warning. Tests: 3 backend tests (matcher cooldown, scope filter, endpoint), all backend (164) and frontend (31) tests green."}}
{"id":"int-dab2e9b9","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-05-15T18:53:25.439181499Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-xza","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"Added schema_drifts table, migration, model, and 30d retention. _diff_event_type_schema detects new_field, missing_field, and type_changed; type_changed only applies to auto-created string/json types, so user-curated enum/number/url/boolean fields are not disturbed. Added a metrics pipeline hook before _ensure_event_type_with_fields. Added GET /event-types/{id}/drifts. EventListItem.drift_count is included through a single-query list_events path. UI adds EventDriftBadge on EventRow with details popover. Tests: drift diff unit test (3 types plus idempotent upsert), all tests green."}}
{"id":"int-349ca4e1","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-05-15T19:20:13.607274865Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-q7a","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"anomaly_context.py: build_sparkline (8-block Unicode, width=24), format_top_movers (signed %, +inf% guard, value truncation), load_top_movers ordered by abs(z_score), and load_recent_metric_points for project_total/event_type/event. Wired through _build_item_template_context -> _build_items_text -> _build_template_context -> _render_delivery_message with optional session+scan_config_id. New vars: sparkline, top_movers, sparkline_line, top_movers_line. Updated default item templates. session.no_autoflush is critical because otherwise SELECT triggers autoflush on the JSON column and loses later in-place payload_snapshot mutations. Tests: 168 backend (+3 explainability), ruff and mypy clean."}}
{"id":"int-be8514ae","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-05-15T19:33:41.551676528Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-p60","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"Fixed by giving the two new migrations unique revision IDs and chaining them after the previous head."}}
